                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3b0d17a5-cf93-4ef1-8afd-747d624585ee",
                        "source_entry_id": "b11765d3-6dc8-3bb1-94d2-c95724eef480",
                        "source_sense_description": "водное морское млекопитающее",
                        "target_lang_word": "killer whale",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "killer whale",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "95f1454f-2ba8-3124-9c9d-f01b9a34c4fb",
                                        "entry_id": "5e048bdd-7dec-33e4-a2ff-34fb5e3005c7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sea mammal related to dolphins and porpoises (Orcinus orca)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "59173142-edc3-4afc-9787-34be7574ee9a",
                                                "sense_id": "95f1454f-2ba8-3124-9c9d-f01b9a34c4fb",
                                                "text": "Of this whale, little is known to the Nantucketer, and nothing at all to the professed naturalist. From what I have seen of him at a distance, I should say that he was about the bigness of a grampus. He is very savage - a sort of Feegee fish. He sometimes takes the great Folio whales by the lip and hangs there like a leech until the mighty brute is worried to death. The killer is never hunted. I have never heard what sort of oil he has. Exception might be taken to the name of this whale, on the grounds of its indistinctness. For we are all killers on land and on sea; Bonaparts and sharks included."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e9410c58-7cc7-4973-975d-be1c740f3eb9",
                                                "sense_id": "95f1454f-2ba8-3124-9c9d-f01b9a34c4fb",
                                                "text": "Once or twice, too, I saw the killer-whale (Orca gladiator), the little species so readily known by its prominent back-fin."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dbacb3d0-6dd9-4b6d-a4a1-0fc0ceaa3462",
                                                "sense_id": "95f1454f-2ba8-3124-9c9d-f01b9a34c4fb",
                                                "text": "It is the killer whale, which follows these herds, makes its attack upon them, and doubtless kills a great many."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "226b81cd-4fee-4e9f-b6d0-22f82c03dcfa",
                                                "sense_id": "95f1454f-2ba8-3124-9c9d-f01b9a34c4fb",
                                                "text": "They display two totems, the Bear and the Killer-Whale (Orca ater) belonging to the Haida-Tsimshian group of tribes, whether Haidas of Queen Charlotte Islands or Tsimshians of the Mainland."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "36b17399-2b37-4d6f-abcd-c2ded152fbb7",
                        "source_entry_id": "b11765d3-6dc8-3bb1-94d2-c95724eef480",
                        "source_sense_description": "водное морское млекопитающее",
                        "target_lang_word": "shamoo",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3299e3c3-0fc4-4a10-ad05-185d0fe76a5b",
                        "source_entry_id": "b11765d3-6dc8-3bb1-94d2-c95724eef480",
                        "source_sense_description": "водное морское млекопитающее",
                        "target_lang_word": "orca",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "orca",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7f2bfeca-f2e0-39dc-abf1-77011cc5ba0c",
                                        "entry_id": "1aa3438b-f104-3db3-aa45-8fd5ca2ec9bf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sea mammal (Orcinus orca) related to dolphins and porpoises, commonly called the killer whale."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "edccb047-6aa2-4654-adf3-9fedefc64f24",
                                                "sense_id": "7f2bfeca-f2e0-39dc-abf1-77011cc5ba0c",
                                                "text": "In the summer, when the weather is calm and beautiful, large flocks of orcæ can be seen approaching the shallow places near the shore, or between the numerous islands of the White Sea. Several fishermen associate for hunting orcæ, each one furnishing a boat, and a large seine made of cords of the thickness of a finger, the meshes being 10½ inches square."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0cb8bd41-5232-45fb-ae18-380d790da2e8",
                        "source_entry_id": "b11765d3-6dc8-3bb1-94d2-c95724eef480",
                        "source_sense_description": "водное морское млекопитающее",
                        "target_lang_word": "Schwertwal",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Schwertwal",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "22286b3e-b322-3194-87bb-fd07a871c1ca",
                                        "entry_id": "f04ccb7c-b0e1-3c2a-95cc-cfc68b60c9ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "schwarzer Wal der Gattung Orcinus orca mit typischem weißen Muster"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c9a52cd0-a85a-4df4-997b-dedd4832b3ea",
                                                "sense_id": "22286b3e-b322-3194-87bb-fd07a871c1ca",
                                                "text": "„Schwertwale jagen wie Wölfe in der Gruppe, wobei zwischen den einzelnen Tieren eine perfekte Abstimmung herrscht.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "92e18135-e680-4728-9b25-470c1fd7f181",
                        "source_entry_id": "b11765d3-6dc8-3bb1-94d2-c95724eef480",
                        "source_sense_description": "водное морское млекопитающее",
                        "target_lang_word": "orque",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "orque",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d6fd92a7-f255-3b31-a6ec-f935812751b9",
                                        "entry_id": "0f90ec9b-4785-3a63-b0e1-28cc6068bbb1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Espèce de grand cétacé à dents à livrée noire et blanche et à nageoire dorsale très haute."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48eeb5eb-6bb6-4165-8251-d1b0b03753f8",
                                                "sense_id": "d6fd92a7-f255-3b31-a6ec-f935812751b9",
                                                "text": "Tout se passa bien ; l’officier de quart n’eut pas le loisir de s’ennuyer : le service l’absorbait et un grand nombre de baleines venaient lui faire visite. Pendant mon quart, un orque passa, avec une grande rapidité, à une très courte distance de la Belgica."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d51546e0-3539-4859-9d86-16579ccc2cbc",
                                                "sense_id": "d6fd92a7-f255-3b31-a6ec-f935812751b9",
                                                "text": "À l’exception d’un Mouton, qui provient des pâturages du mont Pico, et d'une Orque, harponnée en Méditerranée, les autres matériaux d'étude ont été recueillis en plein Atlantique, quelquefois à 1,800 mètres de profondeur."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "751a4f8b-9bec-4ec8-b828-1964db516d28",
                                                "sense_id": "d6fd92a7-f255-3b31-a6ec-f935812751b9",
                                                "text": "Un orque colossal m’avait vu occire son congénère, et était résolu à me le faire payer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43c6eba3-c752-40ad-ba4f-52a4df9e84d3",
                                                "sense_id": "d6fd92a7-f255-3b31-a6ec-f935812751b9",
                                                "text": "Ils firent tant de bruit qu’un orque fut attiré. Les phoques s’enfuirent et Mac eut très peur d’être pris pour un phoque"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "521f5d0d-b920-4436-940c-932d34164f83",
                                                "sense_id": "d6fd92a7-f255-3b31-a6ec-f935812751b9",
                                                "text": "À propos des delphinidés, Pline relate comment un orque fut mis à mort sur l’ordre de l’Empereur Claude"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87e17eda-957f-45c1-b05a-526e19d09c04",
                                                "sense_id": "d6fd92a7-f255-3b31-a6ec-f935812751b9",
                                                "text": "Dans ce cas j’aurais aimé être un orque.\n– Ce n’est pas un poisson mais un mammifère marin.\n– Je le sais, c’était juste pour voir si tu suivais. Oui un orque, ça m’irait très bien."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e29a08d-3707-4692-88e1-c6f889126a9d",
                                                "sense_id": "d6fd92a7-f255-3b31-a6ec-f935812751b9",
                                                "text": "Un jour qu’il mouillait ses filets en haute mer, le pêcheur eut la surprise de rencontrer à nouveau la baleine. Une orque la poursuivait."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "orque",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ba063fb2-a3f5-3c9b-b9b9-58f166692de4",
                                        "entry_id": "76ed1d60-9fc4-3a86-b1f9-cf4cbad4c3ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Variante orthographique de orc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "orque",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a96a290c-72d7-3b1f-8ed3-34d1a9d02547",
                                        "entry_id": "c9f43031-ce4c-3e44-bc8f-76b8ca932b65",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Femme orc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Fantastique"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e4b9191-426d-4d17-a64f-cdec31857153",
                                                "sense_id": "a96a290c-72d7-3b1f-8ed3-34d1a9d02547",
                                                "text": "Son apparence et son caractère se rapprochent désormais plus de ce qu’on pourrait attendre d’une orque."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "be918be0-f306-4017-90a4-a4c2964fcd8c",
                        "source_entry_id": "b11765d3-6dc8-3bb1-94d2-c95724eef480",
                        "source_sense_description": "водное морское млекопитающее",
                        "target_lang_word": "épaulard",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "épaulard",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "75dd7d51-fce0-3c12-997f-806fa1ed165e",
                                        "entry_id": "19d00427-c5f1-37d9-800a-8c26e3debaa9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Grand mammifère marin du sous-ordre des cétacés et de la famille des delphinidés, souvent appelé orque. (Orcinus orca)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Cétologie"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fdc55e4c-cf15-44fb-8df9-5a0e890e0704",
                                                "sense_id": "75dd7d51-fce0-3c12-997f-806fa1ed165e",
                                                "text": "L’épaulard a une réputation de tueur, en fait, il a surtout un solide appétit."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ffc8314c-54c4-4646-b903-7924d83e3287",
                                                "sense_id": "75dd7d51-fce0-3c12-997f-806fa1ed165e",
                                                "text": "L’épaulard a glissé sous notre canot ses huit ou dix tonnes, qu’il manœuvre avec une curiosité intelligente."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e57eae7-4fe3-477b-a74e-fd427089e1fa",
                                                "sense_id": "75dd7d51-fce0-3c12-997f-806fa1ed165e",
                                                "text": "Mais ce jour-là, la faible gîte du bateau, l’air tiède et une troupe d’épaulards dont il observait les sauts distrayèrent^([sic]) son attention pendant qu’il était appuyé à la grande vergue de misaine."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
